{
  "_comment": [
    "THE canonical dispatch-scan-modal → Modal request bodies. One example per",
    "STAGE, both sides. The Deno test (lib.test.ts) asserts the dispatcher builds",
    "a body with exactly each stage's key set; the pytest",
    "(services/scan-modal/tests/test_contract.py) asserts scan_modal's",
    "parse_spawn_body accepts each one and that each stage's job finds its input",
    "keys. Neither side owns the contract, so neither can drift alone — which is",
    "how meshPlyUrl/capturedRoomUrl on one side and meshUrl/capturedRoomJsonUrl",
    "on the other went unnoticed until W1.",
    "W2 note: the envelope (taskId … traceId) is IDENTICAL across stages; only",
    "`inputs` differs, and each stage's inputs are CLOSED — a splat body carries",
    "no meshUrl, a renders body carries no photoUrls. Both sides assert the key",
    "SET, not just its presence, so an extra field is a failure too.",
    "W2 note 2: `renders` builds its scene from capturedRoomJsonUrl and MERGES",
    "glbUrl on top, so captured_room is required and the GLB is optional — the",
    "renders_no_glb variant is the shape a scan with no model_url_gltf gets.",
    "W2 note 3: `splat_config` is the shape a splat task gets when its",
    "agent_tasks payload carries a `config` object. The dispatcher forwards it",
    "VERBATIM and reads nothing inside it; splat_job owns every key's meaning",
    "and its default. A task without one produces the base `splat` shape",
    "unchanged, which is why config lives in a variant and not in the stage.",
    "`variants` holds shapes that are not a stage of their own. splat_rows is",
    "the pose-carrier fallback: the ingest stage strips `photosManifest` as",
    "device-local, so photos_manifest_url is null for a large share of scans and",
    "the dispatcher inlines room_scan_images' own camera_transform /",
    "camera_intrinsics instead. EXACTLY ONE carrier reaches the wire —",
    "photosManifestUrl or photoRecords, never both, never neither — and",
    "photosSource names which.",
    "Dense-frame path (a): splat_keyframes is the shape a scan carrying a",
    "keyframes.tar gets — the base splat body PLUS keyframesArchiveUrl +",
    "keyframeIndexUrl (signed together or not at all) and a config.frameSource.",
    "The dispatcher signs them when scan_bundle_url is set; splat_job's",
    "frameSource (auto|keyframes|photos) decides whether it trains on the dense",
    "100-view RGB stream or the hero photos. A scan without keyframes emits the",
    "base splat shape unchanged.",
    "Every value here is a placeholder; only the SHAPE is normative.",
    "_comment itself is not part of the contract and is ignored by both readers."
  ],
